# Line-ending policy
#
# Store every text file with LF in git AND check it out with LF, on every
# platform. Without this, a contributor whose editor or git config produces
# CRLF commits those bytes verbatim, and the next person to touch the file
# shows a whole-file diff that hides the real change. That happened on
# src/pointcloud_detect/streaming.py: a 2006-line diff for an 88-line change.
#
# `text=auto` = let git detect text vs binary; `eol=lf` = LF in the worktree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats. Marked explicitly rather than relying on git's content
# heuristic, so normalisation can never corrupt them.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary

# Point-cloud data and model artefacts.
*.las   binary
*.laz   binary
*.e57   binary
*.ply   binary
*.pcd   binary
*.npy   binary
*.npz   binary
*.bin   binary
*.pth   binary
*.onnx  binary
